Where Do We Start?
We have used the ASCE definition of an environmental engineer as a starting point for this book:
1. Provision of safe, palatable, and ample public water supplies 2. Proper disposal of or recycling of wastewater and solid wastes 3. Control of water, soil, and atmospheric pollution (including noise as an atmospheric pollutant)


